    "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 2623 reported a net release of $42.6 million in prior year reserves for 2022. This release was primarily driven by favorable development in MAP Risks and Property Risks, partially offset by strengthenings in Cyber Risks and Speciality Risks. The 2020 year of account closed with a gain despite adverse impacts from COVID-19 pandemic losses and natural catastrophes including Hurricanes Ida, Laura, and Storm Uri. The 2021 year of account is forecasting a positive return despite claims from the war in Ukraine and natural catastrophes like Hurricanes Ida, Laura, Storm Uri, Elliot, Volker hail event, and various flooding catastrophes. The overall positive development was attributed to portfolio diversification and careful risk selection.",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
      "released prior year reserves of $42.6m",
      "Net releases are shown by division",
      "gain on capacity of 0.2% having been adversely impacted by the COVID-19 pandemic losses and a number of natural catastrophes, including Hurricanes Ida, Laura and Storm Uri",
      "Beazley has maintained an active approach to portfolio diversification and this coupled with careful risk selection has minimised the impact of these events",
      "forecasting a positive return on capacity of 5.0% having been adversely impacted by claims arising from the war in Ukraine and natural catastrophes such as Hurricane Ida, Hurricane Laura and Storm Uri, among others",
